- Teachers can access only classes and student records for which they have explicit authorization.
- Content editors can manage drafts and submitted content according to their role.
- Only authorized reviewers can approve lessons.
- Only authorized administrators can publish content or manage privileged settings.
- Audit logs cannot be modified by ordinary users.
- Private school and student information is not publicly accessible.

Do not rely solely on frontend checks for security.

Keep the Supabase service-role key and all other privileged secrets out of frontend code and version control.

If privileged operations require Edge Functions, validate the user's identity, permissions, and input on the server.

